      "The Life of Saint Charbel Makhlouf": 1,
      "Saint Charbel Makhlouf (1828-1898) was a Lebanese Maronite monk and priest. Born Youssef in Bekaa Kafra, he entered the Lebanese Maronite Order at 23, lived 23 years as a hermit at Annaya from 1875, and died on Christmas Eve 1898. Paul VI beatified him in 1965 and canonized him on October 9, 1977.": 1,
