      "Annaya online tour": 1,
      "Names and spellings": 1,
      "Charbel, Sharbel, Sarbel and Charbelle all appear. The Syriac form is Mar Sharbel, and Mar is the honorific for a saint. Vatican documents have used Makhlouf, Makhluf and Maklūf. In Latin America he is San Charbel. His baptismal name was Youssef (Joseph).": 1,
      "Birth date.": 1,
      "May 8, 1828 is the traditional date. Santi e Beati says it is \"probably\" May 8 and uncertain. MARI says \"around 1828\" and notes that no authenticated birth certificate has been found.": 1,
      "Ordination.": 1,
      "1859. Some sources give July 23, but the Vatican and MARI give only the year.": 1,
      "Age at death.": 1,
      "70 by calculation and in Paul VI's homily. 68 in the monastery's own death entry.": 1,
      "Years in community.": 1,
      "16 after ordination, as Paul VI says. The Vatican State's Saint of the Day says 15.": 1,
